## Classification-only endpoint correction

The v1 snapshot described visible-failure lifecycle behavior incorrectly and allowed a visible_regression_failed result to count as native-complete without requiring hidden coverage. None of its 16 actual controls took that incomplete path: all visible and hidden populations completed, so every recorded grade remains unchanged. The full v1 snapshot and an additive erratum are retained.

A new v2 service/profile now requires complete designated hidden coverage for any completed grade, including failed visible results. An AST comparison confines the service change to importing and invoking this stricter classifier. Sixteen retained actual population/receipt pairs preserve their grades under the new classifier; eight targeted classification controls cover absent/partial hidden coverage, hidden setup failure, complete visible failure, process failure, timeout, a missing completion signal and an ordinary complete pass. Four supporting public observation patterns verify partial/missing/teardown-error/failed-CALL classification. One actual service startup request with a wrong base was rejected before dispatch. No native suite or public probe was rerun for this classification correction.

The corrected declaration/profile binds this metadata and required coverage. See [classification qualification](candidate_endpoint_v2/classification_qualification_v1/summary.json), [startup control](candidate_endpoint_v2/startup_control_v1/summary.json), and [retained lifecycle erratum](lifecycle_description_erratum_v1.json).
